>>> E9  DISRUPTION - what happens when the plan is wrong?
  CP-SAT is given the PLANNED arrival times and commits to a
  sequence. Rakes then arrive late with probability p. Contract
  Net re-runs its call for proposals every time a line frees, so
  it sees the disruption; the committed schedule does not.
 late_prob  FCFS  FCFS_ci   CNP  CNP_ci  CPSAT  CPSAT_ci
      0.00 44.35    14.03 44.37   14.05  43.47     13.01
      0.20 43.48    14.26 43.54   14.24  42.77     13.01
      0.40 42.66    14.25 42.61   14.07  41.92     12.77
  from 0% to 50% late: CP-SAT degrades -3.6%, CNP -4.0%

